g till that index is at least Q[ i], i.e. (arr[1] & arr[2] &. . .& arr[k] & . . & arr [k]& Q [i]). The basic idea of the approach is to iterate through the array arr[] for every query and find the large index that meets the criteria.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T19:01:44.000Z"},{"id":"sEWLozWVT","title":"Minimize given Number by swapping adjacent digits with odd difference","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/minimize-given-number-by-swapping-adjacent-digits-with-odd-difference/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/minimize-given-number-by-swapping-adjacent-digits-with-odd-difference-sewlozwvt","summary":"Given a string S representing an integer that consists of only characters \u20181\u2019, \u20182\u2019 and \u20183\u2019 the task is to find the smallest number that can be formed from the string. This problem can be easily solved by using the greedy approach using the following observation: 1 and 3 cannot be swapped as their difference is 2 (which is even)","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T18:56:20.000Z"},{"id":"0DzRnt6BY","title":"Reverse given Linked List in groups of specific given sizes","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/reverse-given-linked-list-in-groups-of-specific-given-sizes/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/reverse-given-linked-list-in-groups-of-specific-given-sizes-0dzrnt6by","summary":"Given a linked list and an array arr[] of size N, the task is to reverse every arr[i] nodes of the list at a time (0 \u2264 i < N). If the number of nodes in the list is greater than the sum of array, then the remaining nodes will remain as it is. The solution to the problem is based on the idea of selecting groups of nodes of arr[ i] size.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T18:55:50.000Z"},{"id":"YUZLo627k","title":"Minimum possible sum of absolute difference of pairs from given arrays","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/minimum-possible-sum-of-absolute-difference-of-pairs-from-given-arrays/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/minimum-possible-sum-of-absolute-difference-of-pairs-from-given-arrays-yuzlo627k","summary":"The task is to find the minimum possible sum of absolute difference of pairs formed by pairing each element of array a[] with an element of b[]. Each element of each array can be considered only once. The problem can be efficiently solved by using the concept of dynamic programming using the following idea.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T18:48:42.000Z"},{"id":"dHDhJYJdh","title":"Generate a N sized Array of unique elements with of GCD of adjacent pairs as X","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/generate-a-n-sized-array-of-unique-elements-with-of-gcd-of-adjacent-pairs-as-x/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/generate-a-n-sized-array-of-unique-elements-with-of-gcd-of-adjacent-pairs-as-x-dhdhjyjdh","summary":"Given two integers N (always even) and X, the task is to find an array of numbers such that the sum of GCD of adjacent pairs (where each element is part of only one pair) is X. If no such array is possible return -1. If there are more than 1 possible sequence return any of them.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T18:40:59.000Z"},{"id":"GjmIKtN90","title":"Check if given Trees can be made mirror images of each other in K swaps","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/check-if-given-trees-can-be-made-mirror-images-of-each-other-in-k-swaps/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/check-if-given-trees-can-be-made-mirror-images-of-each-other-in-k-swaps-gjmiktn90","summary":"Given two binary tree with same structure but may have different arrangement of value and given an integer K. The task is to check that after exactly K swap on first tree, will it become mirror of second one. The idea is to traverse the first tree and check by swapping nodes recursively, if the tree becomes mirror image of second tree.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T18:40:38.000Z"},{"id":"joNHGcZ9L","title":"Rearrange given Array such that all set bit positions have higher value than others","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/rearrange-given-array-such-that-all-set-bit-positions-have-higher-value-than-others/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/rearrange-given-array-such-that-all-set-bit-positions-have-higher-value-than-others-jonhgcz9l","summary":"Given an array B1[] and a binary array B2[] each of size N, the task is to rearrange B1[i] in a way such that for all setbit position i of B2[i], the value of B1 [i] will be greater than the values where bit is not set in B2:[i] i.e for all (i, j) B1,[i] > B1.[j] when B2 [i]. = 1, B2,[j] = 0 (0 \u2264 i, j < N).","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T18:08:23.000Z"},{"id":"YTrevypix","title":"OSSeeD Technologies LLP Interview Experience for Software Engineer","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/osseed-technologies-llp-interview-experience-for-software-engineer/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/osseed-technologies-llp-interview-experience-for-software-engineer-ytrevypix","summary":"There are two rounds. The first one is aptitude and logical round and the second and the last one is HR round. The questions were not very difficult but were very tricky. The technical aptitude part covered questions from data structures & algorithms, Databases, and questions for writing down programs, SQL queries.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T17:11:55.000Z"},{"id":"ZO_zlRh_l","title":"Paytm Interview Experience for Data Engineer ( 2 Years Experienced)","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/paytm-interview-experience-for-data-engineer-2-years-experienced/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/paytm-interview-experience-for-data-engineer-2-years-experienced--zo-zlrh-l","summary":"The interview process for a new Python developer starts with a 1hr round of questions. The questions are easy to difficult level and range from the technical to the management level. The interview will be followed by a 3hr managerial round. The interviewer will then go on to the next round of the interview.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc19a6a0c6","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-07T17:09:34.000Z"},{"id":"KKu2ejUGt","title":"Quantiphi Interview Experience for ChatBot Engineer (On-Campus)","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/quantiphi-interview-experience-for-chatbot-engineer-on-campus/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/quantiphi-interview-experience-for-chatbot-engineer-on-campus--kku2ejugt","summary":"The test had 7 sections which had the quantitative aptitude, qualitative aptitude and logical reasoning as sections. The DSA interviewer first asked a basic array-based question and then asked my approach for a medium-level (going by gfg standards) string question. The interviewer was friendly and promptly communicated when I explained my approach.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f7eed3a950f44813694fa9fc1